# Build context for deploy/witness/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context
# root's `.dockerignore`, so this scopes the exclusions to this build without
# changing what any other Dockerfile in the repository sees.
#
# The build context is the repository root, because the image builds the
# workspace. Without this file that context includes `target/`, which is tens
# of gigabytes of build output on a developer machine -- all of it uploaded to
# the daemon and none of it used, since the image compiles from source.
#
# Kept deliberately short. Every entry is either build output or a directory no
# workspace member reads, and the list is not extended for image size: an
# exclusion that turns out to be wrong shows up as a confusing compile error
# inside a container, which is a bad trade for a few megabytes of context.

# Build output.
target/
**/target/

# Not read by the build. The commit is passed in as TRACE_COMMONS_BUILD_COMMIT
# instead of resolved from .git -- the same route Cloud Build takes, and the
# reason `trace-commons-build-info` prefers that variable over `git rev-parse`.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.superpowers/

# The desktop shells. Neither is a workspace member (see the root Cargo.toml's
# `members`), so neither is compiled by this build.
macos/
windows/
